# Every pull request gets @fyannk as a reviewer automatically.
#
# The repository rule on main requires zero approvals, so this does not
# gate merging; it exists so review is requested without anyone having to
# remember to ask, and so the owner of each area is written down rather
# than known.
*                           @fyannk

# The trust boundary. Authorization, the forwarded-header contract, the
# CSRF and operation guards, and the RBAC the console runs under are the
# places where a wrong change is a security change rather than a bug.
/internal/authz/            @fyannk
/internal/identity/         @fyannk
/internal/ops/              @fyannk
/internal/redact/           @fyannk
/deploy/                    @fyannk
/SECURITY.md                @fyannk

# Publishing and supply chain: anything here decides what gets built,
# signed, attested, and pushed under the project's name.
/.github/workflows/         @fyannk
/Dockerfile                 @fyannk
/Makefile                   @fyannk
/hack/                      @fyannk
/third_party/               @fyannk
